        "note": "For $g(x)=a\\sqrt{b(x-h)}+k$, a parent input u maps to $x=h+u/b$ and its y-value maps to $k+a\\sqrt{u}$."
      },
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "p0",
          "label": "Image of $(0,0)$",
          "inputProfile": "orderedPair",
          "expected": "({{h}},{{k}})"
        },
        {
          "id": "p4",
          "label": "Image of $(4,2)$",
          "inputProfile": "orderedPair",
          "expected": "({{x4}},{{y4}})"
        },
        {
          "id": "p16",
          "label": "Image of $(16,4)$",
          "inputProfile": "orderedPair",
          "expected": "({{x16}},{{y16}})"
        },
        {
          "id": "vertical-scale",
          "label": "Vertical compression scale factor",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "0.5"
        },
        {
          "id": "horizontal-scale",
          "label": "Horizontal compression scale factor",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "0.25"
        },
        {
          "id": "horizontal-reflection",
          "label": "Effect of the negative inside factor",
          "inputProfile": "choice",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "horizontal",
              "label": "Horizontal reflection; the ray extends left from the endpoint."
            },
            {
              "id": "xaxis",
              "label": "Reflection across the x-axis."
            },
            {
              "id": "none",
              "label": "No reflection."
            }
          ],
          "expected": "horizontal"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Point mapping makes horizontal compression/reflection and vertical compression visible.",
        "reasoning": [
          "Because b=-4, parent inputs are divided by -4 before adding h. That compresses horizontal distances by 1/4 and reverses their direction.",
          "Because a=0.5, vertical distances from k are halved.",
          "The endpoint remains $({{h}},{{k}})$ and the transformed ray extends left."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "Mapped points $({{h}},{{k}})$, $({{x4}},{{y4}})$, $({{x16}},{{y16}})$; vertical factor 1/2, horizontal factor 1/4, horizontal reflection."
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "For the x-coordinate mapping, divide the parent input by b before adding h."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "A negative b reverses horizontal direction. The magnitude |b|=4 compresses horizontal distances to one fourth."
      ],
